  "interpretation": [
    "For this source-pinned cohort, retrieval exposed the expected target in 29/30 searches. Of 28 selections, 24 were wholly inside an accepted target range and 26 intersected one; strict full-range equality was only 8/30, a metric that misses narrower relevant blocks.",
    "The blind Luna review judged 26/28 fetched excerpts to answer their query fully, one partial, and one unsupported. This is useful semantic diagnostic evidence, not owner-gold or an independent-human quality estimate.",
    "15/28 fetched excerpts were rated medium or high overbreadth, so answer coverage does not yet imply focused retrieval. The 17 packs that the original runner constructed validated; the 11 ranges blocked by the false-negative fetch validator have no pack result and remain unmeasured.",
    "Choice and evidence-sufficiency values remain descriptive and uncalibrated. Thirty distinct sourceRefs do not establish statistical independence; these labels and documents have prior development exposure.",
    "The run tests explicit-source search, Jev selection, exact fetch, and verbatim evidence packing. It does not test global discovery, metadata-filter quality, multi-range union, compaction, synthesis/paragraph composition, or calibrated confidence."
  ],
